      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most effective approach is to integrate both national triumphs and systemic injustices, as they complement rather than compete with each other in providing a balanced historical narrative. Focusing solely on triumphs risks creating an overly idealized view, while concentrating exclusively on injustices may alienate some students if diversity and civic pride aren't also addressed. Research on middle school engagement suggests that students learn best when they are asked to analyze both successes and failures to develop critical thinking skills regarding complex societal structures.",
